    "narrative": "The core of today\u2019s offensive attack is anchored by **Jos\u00e9 Ram\u00edrez**, who boasts the day\u2019s high-water mark of 85.92. He profiles as an elite play against Young, benefiting from a massive +16% park factor and favorable SP skill metrics. Joining him in the top tier is **Lawrence Butler** (73.17), whose matchup against Jos\u00e9 Soriano offers an excellent combination of park advantage and a +13% platoon boost, making him a prime candidate for production. **Bryce Harper** (71.72) and **Jonathan Aranda** (70.47) also project as strong starts, with **Jonathan Aranda** capitalizing on an elite +19% SP skill rating against the vulnerable AJ Smith-Shawver. We are also monitoring **Dylan Beavers** (68.38), whose matchup is bolstered by a favorable park and, crucially, a slow opposing pitcher delivery that should facilitate his stolen base potential\u2014a vital component given our focus on speed.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved the benching of Braden Montgomery, who posted a respectable 53.28 score. Ultimately, the optimizer favored **Dylan Beavers** and **Justin Crawford** due to their higher raw utility and more favorable platoon positioning. While **Gleyber Torres** (51.57) was considered, his heavy negative platoon adjustment against Kremer forced him to the bench in favor of the higher-ceiling options currently slotted in our MI and UTIL spots. \n\nWe are proceeding with caution regarding the \u201cLineup Pending\u201d status for several key contributors, most notably **Cal Raleigh** and **Zack Gelof**. **Cal Raleigh** remains a marginal play at 58.04, and any drop in his batting order could further compress his daily efficiency. While we are confident in the setup for **Will Smith** against Nick Lodolo, we are tracking the weather and late-inning bullpen usage carefully, as any shift in the leverage environment could impact the SB opportunities we are banking on from players like **Dylan Beavers** and **Justin Crawford**.",
